const overview = `<section id="overview" class="divider">${H.sectionLabel('The Plan at a Glance','Cold drama, then warm water','The route uses Icelandair’s stopover structure and protects the Italy half for repeated 74–77°F swims.')}<div class="overview"><div class="ocard"><p class="eyebrow">Route</p><h4>PIT → KEF → FCO</h4><p>Four Iceland nights, then three Forio nights and a four-night Cilento road base.</p></div><div class="ocard"><p class="eyebrow">Warm-water rule</p><h4>Italy carries every sea swim</h4><p>Iceland water is geothermal only. Ischia and Cilento still carry seven nights of warm Tyrrhenian beach time.</p></div><div class="ocard"><p class="eyebrow">Operational design</p><h4>FCO buffer night</h4><p>The final night protects the June 23 flight and can still support a short Rome evening when the drive arrives early.</p></div><div class="ocard"><p class="eyebrow">Readiness</p><h4>Not ready to book</h4><p>2027 exact PIT–KEF and KEF–FCO operating days, the stopover fare, and all live quotes require recheck.</p></div></div><div class="tldr"><b>TL;DR:</b> the fourth Iceland night buys genuine weather insurance without adding a thirteenth hotel night. The cost is one less Ischia day; La Mortella is no longer a standalone anchor, while the warm-water flagship at Negombo remains protected.</div></section>`;
